== Part B: real git repos, real commits, real tags -- the pin/diff/compose wiring ==
-- building a throwaway platform repo: v0.1.0 (2.0.0 + 3.0.0 live), v1.0.0 (2.0.0 retired) --
-- building the matching throwaway ludlow repo: base pins v0.1.0, head pins v1.0.0 --

B1. retirement -> composed MAJOR -> the pull request check must fail (no cosign needed: the retired version has no evidence to look up)
REFUSE: composed bump is major -- ['2.0.0']
OK: retirement of 2.0.0 correctly refused the pull request check, comment names it

B2. resolved-commit mismatch -> refuse (ADR-0001's pin made load-bearing, bug #2)
REFUSE: platform tag 'v1.0.0' resolves to '2bbf35a29213b6c0d4e1416d892323714863d5ad', but platform-pin.yaml pins commit 'cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc' -- refusing (ADR-0001's pin is load-bearing, not decorative)
OK: a pin naming the wrong commit for a real tag is refused, real git rev-parse caught it

B3. composed weaker than the publisher's tag (unchanged array, major tag jump) -> informational, exit 0, never lowers
INFO: composed bump (none) is weaker than the publisher's tag bump (major, v0.1.0 -> v1.0.0) -- informational only, never lowers what this institution treats as the obligation.
PASS: declared=major composed=none
OK: composed=none against declared=major (v0.1.0 -> v1.0.0) passes, prints informational, never fails

